A field the new version declares by name, beneath a struct the lens does
not map, that the old version accepted only through ...: the source has no
field of that name to copy, and the struct still accepts fields it does not
name, so the struct is copied whole and reported as a whole. A copy field by
field would copy owner alone, and drop size and every other field without an
error.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		...
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size?: int
		...
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		id: v0_0.id
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size?: int
		...
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0358]: the ForwardLens in history/1.0.thema would copy v0_0.meta into meta, which does not accept every value of it
  --> history/1.0.thema:10:1
   |
10 | ForwardLens: {
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: both 0.0 and 1.0 declare meta, so a lens that does not map it copies it
   = note: meta.size in 1.0 is now int, which does not accept every value of the prior _
   = help: map meta in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant
